chore: split long functions instead of allowing too_many_lines

Pedantic clippy flagged bash(), exec(), to_openai_chat_messages, and
resumed_compaction_restores_summarized_message_count over the 100-line
limit. Each had clear seams, so extract helpers rather than opt out
with #[allow]: bash() gains command_for and bash_result_json, exec()
gains install_cpu_guard, to_openai_chat_messages breaks into per-role
pushers, and the test gains seed_compacted_turn and
seed_post_compact_continuation.

The remaining pedantic lints are mechanical: missing backticks on
QuickJS and on a quoted error string, ExecCtx::Debug ending in
finish() (intentional — closures are omitted; switched to
finish_non_exhaustive), a format!-inside-collect in a test now going
through fold + writeln!, and two test apps rebuilt as let instead of
let mut.